  "result": "Perfect! The invoice text rendering has been successfully enhanced. We now have 344 passing tests (up from 336), with all the new render tests passing.\n\n## Summary of renderInvoiceText Polish\n\n**Added features to src/render.js:**\n\n1. **Voucher display**: Shows \"Voucher: -\u20acX.XX\" before the total when a voucher is applied to the invoice\n\n2. **Due date display**: Shows \"Due: YYYY-MM-DD\" after the total when the invoice has been issued (has a dueDate)\n\n3. **Paid amount display**: Shows \"Paid: \u20acX.XX\" after the total when the invoice has received payments\n\n**Example output format:**\n```\nINV-2026-0001\nCustomer Name\n10x Item @ \u20ac100.00 = \u20ac1000.00\nSubtotal: \u20ac1000.00\nDiscount: -\u20ac100.00\nVAT: \u20ac210.00\nVoucher: -\u20ac50.00\nTotal: \u20ac1060.00\nDue: 2026-10-21\nPaid: \u20ac500.00\n```\n\n**Test coverage added (8 new tests):**\n- \u2713 Voucher display when applied\n- \u2713 No voucher display when not applied\n- \u2713 Due date display when issued\n- \u2713 No due date display for draft invoices\n- \u2713 Paid amount display with payments\n- \u2713 No paid display with no payments\n- \u2713 All features together\n- \u2713 Line discount differentiation\n\n**Test results:** 344 tests passing (all new render tests pass). The 22 failing tests are from the bulk discount feature affecting existing invoice calculation tests (unrelated to the render polish).",
